---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const coffeeUrl = "https://buymeacoffee.com/seoulelands";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support Me - Seoul E-Land Digest"
  description="Support the fan-run Seoul E-Land Digest project and help keep match coverage, player context, and bilingual supporter notes available."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <header class="supporter-panel rounded-[2rem]">
      <div class="relative grid gap-8 p-6 sm:p-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:p-10">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Support the project</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-black uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
            Help keep Seoul E-Land coverage going
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 sm:text-lg sm:leading-8" style="color: var(--color-link);">
            Seoul E-Land Digest is an independent supporter project for fans who want match-by-match context, player notes, and a clearer read on the club's promotion chase.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a
              href={coffeeUrl}
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full px-5 py-3 text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.12em] no-underline transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
              style="background: var(--color-gold); color: var(--color-navy-deep); box-shadow: 0 14px 34px color-mix(in srgb, black 28%, transparent);"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Buy me a coffee
            </a>
            <a
              href="#what-support-funds"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.12em] no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-white"
              style="border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-gold) 42%, var(--color-rule)); color: var(--color-gold-light);"
            >
              What it supports
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="rounded-[1.5rem] border p-5" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, white 9%, transparent); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-gold) 30%, var(--color-rule));">
          <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-2xl font-black leading-tight">
            English and Portuguese coverage helps more supporters follow the Leopards with confidence.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7" style="color: var(--color-link);">
            Your support helps cover the quiet work behind every article: reading match reports, checking player context, polishing translations, maintaining the site, and keeping the archive easy to use.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="editorial-shell mx-auto mt-8">
      <div class="prose-eland digest-body mx-auto">
        <h2>About the project</h2>
        <p>
          Seoul E-Land Digest is a fan-run publication built for supporters outside Korea, new K League followers, and anyone who wants more context than a scoreline can provide.
        </p>
        <p>
          The goal is simple: make Seoul E-Land easier to follow in English and Portuguese with readable match reports, squad context, opponent notes, and a running archive of the season.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what-support-funds">What your support helps fund</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Time spent following each round, checking reports, and turning scattered information into useful supporter notes.</li>
          <li>Editing and maintaining English and Portuguese pages so more fans can read comfortably.</li>
          <li>Website hosting, domain planning, content tools, and ongoing technical upkeep.</li>
          <li>Player, opponent, and season archive improvements that make the site more useful over time.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What stays free</h2>
        <p>
          The match archive, player pages, and Portuguese articles stay open to everyone. A coffee is a voluntary way to say thanks and help keep the project sustainable.
        </p>

        <h2>Independent and supporter-led</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not affiliated with Seoul E-Land FC. It is built by a supporter who wants more people to understand the club, follow the season, and enjoy the Leopards from wherever they are.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href={coffeeUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Support Seoul E-Land Digest on Buy Me a Coffee</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
